# AI Trek Explorer currently uses only free, key-free APIs:
#   - Nominatim (geocoding)
#   - OSRM demo server (routing)
#   - Open-Meteo (weather + elevation)
#   - Overpass API (places along the route)
#
# No environment variables are required to run the app as shipped.
#
# If you later swap in a key-gated provider (e.g. a paid routing service,
# a commercial weather API, or an AI API like Gemini/OpenAI for richer
# insight text), add the key here — never hardcode it in a component —
# and read it via import.meta.env.VITE_xxx. Vite only exposes variables
# prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and anything exposed to the browser
# is visible to users, so a key that must stay secret (e.g. a paid AI API
# key) should be called from a small backend/proxy instead of directly
# from this frontend.

# VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY=
# VITE_ROUTING_API_KEY=
# VITE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# VITE_AI_API_KEY=
